This auto-integration branch HEAD did not build before this change, for reasons unrelated to the surface:
1. apps/windows/TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj was corrupt again — TWO concatenated <Project>
   roots (MSB4025 "multiple root elements" at line 1103) with five </Project> closers and 1183 <Compile> lines
   for only 391 distinct linked sources (~3x duplication from repeated bad integration merges). The two roots
   were also DIVERGENT (19 links existed only in the stale first root: AlertsSection, BatteryHealthSection,
   BatteryPill, EnvironmentSlide, HighlightCard, OverviewTab*, OverviewVehicleComparison*, PatternsSlide*,
   SavingsSlide*, SlideRenderer, StatChartSlide), so neither root was a superset. Repaired in place: collapsed
   to one valid root holding the deduplicated UNION of all 391 distinct <Compile> links (each verified to exist
   on disk -> 0 stale), normalized to LF, and added the new SummaryStatsGrid links. No test coverage dropped
   (8739 headless tests pass, vs 8388 at the 0078 baseline + surfaces added since); the same corruption was
   repaired identically by feature-view 0078 before a later merge re-introduced it.

### Surface deliverable (feature-views/SummaryStatsGrid/)
SummaryStatsGrid.Model.cs / .Source.cs / .ViewModel.cs / .cs + Tests/FeatureViews/SummaryStatsGridTests.cs
(26 test cases). Parity port of web SummaryStatsGrid.tsx: TsFadeIn (delay 0.05s) over a responsive 2/3/6-column
grid of six glass-panel summary cards (Total Sessions / Total Energy / Avg Charge Rate / Peak Rate / Avg
Duration / Total Cost), each an uppercase label + value + optional unit suffix (kWh/kW/min hard-coded like the
web). The cards' figures reproduce the web Charging-Curve page useMemo reduction verbatim (Total Energy sums
total_energy_added_wh and is labeled kWh exactly as the web grid does; avg/peak rate from peak_power_w/1000;
avg duration from per-session whole minutes). Full native state matrix: loading (per-card skeletons, the web
SummaryCard loading branch) / loaded / empty (zeroed cards, never a blank box) / error (retry surface) / stale
/ offline (freshness chip + refresh). Data via GET /charging-sessions through the shared cache-then-network
engine (no HTTP in the view). All six source i18n keys resolve in Strings/*/Resources.resw
(translation.charging.curve.{totalSessions,totalEnergy,avgChargeRate,peakRate,avgDuration,totalCost}); native
chrome reuses existing common.{loading,offline,refresh,retry} + charging.curve.{title} keys. Narrator names on
every card and interactive element; reduce-motion honoured via TsFadeIn; view.opened slug=SummaryStatsGrid.

